#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lommel_t2

#% text
# `lommel_t2(mu, nu, z)` gives the modified Lommel function `T_(mu, nu)(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `T_(mu, nu)(z) = -t_(mu, nu)(z) + 2^(mu - 1) gamma((mu - nu + 1)/2) gamma((mu + nu + 1)/2) (I_nu(z) + (sin(mu pi) + sin(nu pi))/pi K_nu(z))`, the solution of `z^2 w'' + z w' - (z^2 + nu^2) w = -z^(mu + 1)` with the expansion `z^(mu - 1) (1 + ((mu - 1)^2 - nu^2)/z^2 + ...)` at infinity.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lommel_t2(-0.25, 2/3, 1)
#% output
#= 0.8381911675400365

#% cell
n(lommel_t2(2, 3/2, 4), 30)
#% output
#= 3.7165183624360502655026928435275547

#% cell
lommel_t2(7/3 + im, 1.2, 4.5 - im)
#% output
#= 2.019192068961997 + 8.768166584832779im

#% cell
lommel_t2(1/2, 1/3, [0.5, 1.0, 1.5])
#% output
#= [1.344734510834332, 1.0045367136617995, 0.8318547713759533]

#% text
# At `mu = 2`, `nu = 5` the expansion at infinity terminates: `z (1 - 24/z^2 + 576/z^4 - 9216/z^6)`:

#% cell
lommel_t2(2, 5, z)
#% output
#= z - 9216/z^5 - 24/z + 576/z^3

